    "seconds": 46,
    "summary": "The fault was a fault-injection flag left on by default. I set it back to off, and the pods are healthy.\n\n**Root cause:** The `flagd-config` ConfigMap had `productCatalogFailure` with `defaultVariant: \"on\"`. Upstream ships this flag as `off`. With it on, product-catalog fails requests for a specific product. Flagd had just restarted, so the bad default was picked up by the new pods.\n\n**Change made:**\n- Set `productCatalogFailure.defaultVariant` to `\"off\"` in the `flagd-config` ConfigMap. Nothing else in the file changed.\n- Restarted `deploy/flagd` so its init container copied the corrected file into the pod. The init container's log confirms the copy has `\"defaultVariant\": \"off\"`.\n\n**Verification:**\n- All 29 pods in `astronomy-shop` are Running and fully ready, with zero restarts.\n- I did not run an end-to-end request against product-catalog, since flagd's image has no shell or wget to query it.\n\n**Not changed:** The product-catalog deployment spec is identical to its previous revision. The only difference is a restart annotation.",
